 "id": "2026-11-23-baltic-ship-drone-strike",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "A burning Russian ship drifted into NATO waters. Is the Baltic the next front?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Russian officials say two drones hit the cargo ship Sparta Two on Saturday, west of Gogland island. It was bound for Kaliningrad. Finland's military says the ship caught fire and drifted into Finnish waters. The crew was evacuated."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Who sent the drones? Finland says the attack was likely Ukrainian. Kyiv has not claimed it. The ship is sanctioned by the U.S. and Ukraine and belongs to Russia's defence ministry. Earlier this month, Ukraine's security service claimed a strike on a Russian warship nearby."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Finland informed NATO and brought back air and sea restrictions in the eastern Gulf. President Stubb called the incident serious. On Sunday, Finland says, a Russian rescue vessel began towing the ship out of Finnish waters."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will the Baltic see another drone strike before New Year? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
